# Web3Forms access key for the contact form.
#
# Create one free at https://web3forms.com using the inbox you actually read —
# Web3Forms delivers to whichever address the key was registered under, and
# that cannot be overridden from the request.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is deliberate. Web3Forms rejects server-side submissions on the
# free plan ("Use our API in client side..."), so the form posts from the
# browser. Their access keys are public by design: scoped to one inbox,
# rate-limited, and restrictable by domain in the dashboard. It is not a secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=your-web3forms-access-key
